from now on, use integers instead of floats
(=============================================================================)
(                  APEX-Z  - v7.1 : NATIVE ZOOMY CHESS ENGINE                  )
(          Compiles to a zero-dependency static x86-64 Linux ELF              )
(                                                                             )
(  v2.1 was the Zoomy 5.1 rewrite: loops, functions with parameters and       )
(  recursion.  v3.0 adds a real search: iterative deepening, aspiration       )
(  windows, principal-variation search, a transposition table, null-move      )
(  pruning, late-move reductions and pruning, futility, reverse-futility and   )
(  razoring, check extensions, a quiescence search with delta and SEE         )
(  pruning, and killer / history move ordering.  v3.1 adds a much richer       )
(  evaluation: pawn structure, passed pawns, bishop pair, rook files, king     )
(  safety and endgame kings, drawn endings; mate distance pruning and          )
(  internal iterative reduction.  v4: UCI and Polyglot books.  v5: magic          )
(  bitboards.  v6.0: tapered evaluation with safe mobility, king safety and a   )
(  pawn cache; two-entry TT buckets with ageing and a Hash option; history      )
(  gravity, continuation history and capture history shared between the         )
(  helper threads, staged move generation; singular extensions with multi-cut  )
(  and double extensions; PV-stability and node-based time control; automatic   )
(  depth 14 / 13 / 17 plies opening / middlegame / endgame, optional PEXT      )
(  v7.1: static exchange evaluation (SEE) prunes losing captures and late losing   )
(  captures are reduced, +45 +- 39 Elo over 200 games, on by default.            )
(  v7.0 (Zoomy 8.1): an optional NNUE (HalfKAv2) that adds to the evaluation, see   )
(  the NNUE section and the nnue folder; Features 1048576 lifts the 22 ply search   )
(  limit to 60, 2097152 is a modern pruning set - neither measured stronger, so   )
(  both are off.  The UCI option Features is a sum of bits: 1 2 4 8 64 128     )
(  the older search features, 256 singular, 512 tapered eval, 1024 safe       )
(  mobility, 2048 king safety, 4096 pawn cache, 8192 new history, 16384 staged  )
(  moves, 32768 double extensions, 65536 node-based time, 131072 PV stability,  )
(  524288 PEXT, needs BMI2.                                                    )
(=============================================================================)

(--- 1. Mailbox board  - 10x12: playable squares are 21..28, 31..38, ... 91..98 ---)
(    White pieces are positive, black negative: 1 pawn, 2 knight, 3 bishop,)
(    4 rook, 5 queen, 6 king.  99 marks the border around the board.)
Create an array named board with 120 slots

(Direction offsets: 0-7 knight, 8-15 king and queen, 16-19 rook, 20-23 bishop.)
Create an array named dirs with 24 slots

(Piece letters  - as character codes and values, indexed by piece type 0..6.)
Create an array named letters with 7 slots
Create an array named piece_value with 7 slots
Create an array named back_rank with 8 slots

(Castling rights: white kingside, white queenside, black kingside, black queenside.)
(corner_sq holds the rook's starting square for each right.)
Create an array named castle with 4 slots
Create an array named corner_sq with 4 slots

(--- 2. Move buffers: ply p keeps its moves in slots  - p-1*256 ..  - p-1*256+255 ---)
Create an array named mv_from with 18432 slots
Create an array named mv_to with 18432 slots
Create an array named mv_score with 18432 slots
Create an array named mv_count with 72 slots

