(position hash numbers)
Create an array named zob with 1560 slots
(transposition table, shared by every search thread (Zoomy 5.5 shared arrays).)
(An entry is two numbers: tt_a packs move + 16384 * (depth + 64 * (bound + 4 * (score + 100000)))   )
(and age; two entries make a bucket: the first is depth-preferred, the second always replaced.)
(with bound 0 exact, 1 score is at least, 2 score is at most; tt_b holds key - tt_a.  A reader   )
(accepts an entry only if tt_b + tt_a equals its key, so an entry two threads wrote half each is  )
(thrown away instead of trusted.)
(room for 256 MB of table; only the part the Hash option asks for is ever touched)
Create a shared array named tt_a with 16777216 slots
Create a shared array named tt_b with 16777216 slots
Let a number be called tt_buckets
Let a number be called tt_age
Let a number be called tt_mb
